# Write a skill — always apply

Before adding a file under `.agents/skills/`, or renaming, moving, or materially editing one — in
this repository or any repository it routes to — read and apply
[`write-skill/SKILL.md`](../skills/write-skill/SKILL.md): confirm a skill is the right artifact,
place it in the owning repository, and follow the stated layout (`.agents/skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md`,
hyphen-separated, frontmatter `name` matching the directory) rather than inventing a local variant.

The trigger is the file path, not the size of the edit: a skill is discovered by its frontmatter, so
a one-line description change is a change to when every future agent loads it.

## Forbidden

- A new skill whose path, name, or frontmatter departs from the convention without the loader-level
  reason the skill names.
- Renaming, moving, or removing a skill without updating every reference to it, and its entry in
  the owning repository's `AGENTS.md` index where that file keeps one, in the same change.
- Adding a skill for something that is an always-on constraint (a rule), durable domain knowledge (a
  reference), or a one-time record (a PR, ticket, or dated doc).
